# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# Why the working tree too (`-text` would only do the repository): the site is deployed
# with `vercel build --prebuilt`, i.e. the dist that goes live is built on whichever
# machine runs the deploy, while CI builds on Linux. When Windows checked these files
# out as CRLF the two builds diverged, and a parser bug that CI could never see shipped
# the story title twice on every story page. Same bytes everywhere, same dist everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.mp4 binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
